WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.120
Picture every teenager in the UK, from
one end of the country to the other.

2
00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:07.850
You want to find out
something about all of them.

3
00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:09.620
But you can't test them all.

4
00:00:09.670 --> 00:00:13.410
So you zoom in on one
classroom: 20 people,

5
00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:14.970
right in front of you.

6
00:00:15.020 --> 00:00:19.970
Can those 20 classmates really speak
for every teenager in the country?

7
00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:22.950
In this mission, you'll
meet the target population,

8
00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:26.000
the whole group a researcher
wants to find out about,

9
00:00:26.050 --> 00:00:28.640
and the sample who take part.

10
00:00:28.690 --> 00:00:31.330
You'll find out what makes
a sample representative,

11
00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:33.730
so its findings can be generalised.

12
00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:36.790
And you'll compare two
ways of choosing people:

13
00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:39.550
random and opportunity sampling.

14
00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:43.290
Your mission: decide whether
20 classmates are enough,

15
00:00:43.340 --> 00:00:44.510
and explain why.
